# Optional overrides for local development.
#
# You do not need this file to run Orbit. `make setup` generates a .env with the
# machine-local secrets, and every other value has a default: compose settings in
# docker-compose.yml, and in-cluster settings in deploy/local/orbit-values.yaml.
#
# Copy a line into .env only when you need to change it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bedrock (optional). Enables the Bedrock provider in the inference gateway.
# `make cluster-bedrock-creds` reads these to refresh the cluster's credentials
# from your local AWS SSO session.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BEDROCK_ENABLED=true
# AWS_PROFILE=orbit
# BEDROCK_REGION=us-east-1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backing services. Defaults live in docker-compose.yml. Override only if the
# ports collide with something else on your machine.
#
# Changing DB_PASSWORD after the first `make up` will not work: Postgres bakes
# the password into its volume at first initialisation. Run `make dev-down-clean`
# to drop the volume first.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DB_PORT=5432
# DB_USER=orbit
# DB_NAME=orbit
# DB_PASSWORD=orbit
# REDIS_PORT=6379
# REDIS_PASSWORD=orbit

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tenant used by `make auth`. Defaults to `example`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ORBIT_TENANT_ID=example
